---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import FlightCostEstimator from '../../components/tools/FlightCostEstimator.jsx';

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebApplication',
  name: 'Flight Cost Estimator',
  applicationCategory: 'TravelApplication',
  operatingSystem: 'Any',
  offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0' },
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Flight Cost Estimator from Pakistan — KHI, LHE, ISB Return Fares"
  description="Estimate return flight costs from Karachi, Lahore, Islamabad to Dubai, London, New York, Istanbul, Bangkok and 20+ routes."
  schema={schema}
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
    <nav class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Home</a> ›
      <a href="/tools/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Tools</a> ›
      <span>Flight Cost Estimator</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Flight Cost Estimator</h1>
    <p class="text-gray-700 mb-8">
      Rough return fare estimates from Pakistan to popular destinations. Factors in season, cabin class, and booking window.
    </p>

    <FlightCostEstimator client:load />

    <section class="prose max-w-none mt-12">
      <h2>How to Get Better Fares from Pakistan</h2>

      <h3>Book 2–3 Months Ahead for Long-Haul</h3>
      <p>
        Fares to Europe, North America, and Australia are typically cheapest when booked 8–12 weeks out. Last-minute bookings (within 2 weeks) can cost 50% more. For Gulf and Southeast Asia, the window is tighter — 4–8 weeks ahead.
      </p>

      <h3>Fly Mid-Week</h3>
      <p>
        Tuesday and Wednesday departures are consistently cheaper than Friday–Sunday. For returns, mid-week is also better. Return on a Tuesday rather than Monday to save noticeably.
      </p>

      <h3>Use Multi-City or Open-Jaw</h3>
      <p>
        Flying into one European city and out of another can be cheaper than return to the same city — plus you see more. Skyscanner "Everywhere" search is useful for this.
      </p>

      <h3>Consider Gulf Hubs</h3>
      <p>
        Dubai, Abu Dhabi, Doha are major hubs with competitive fares to Europe and the Americas. Pakistani travellers often save by taking a cheap Gulf-sector flight (Emirates, Etihad, Qatar, Saudia) and booking separately.
      </p>

      <h3>Peak Season Awareness</h3>
      <p>
        Fares spike for:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>May–August:</strong> school holidays, European summer</li>
        <li><strong>Hajj season (May–June):</strong> Jeddah/Madinah fares double</li>
        <li><strong>December:</strong> Christmas, winter holidays, Umrah peak</li>
        <li><strong>Eid holidays:</strong> inflated Pakistan ↔ Gulf fares for 1–2 weeks</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Direct vs Connecting Flights</h2>
      <p>
        Pakistan has limited direct long-haul connectivity. Most trips to Europe/North America require a connection in the Gulf. Common connecting hubs:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Dubai (DXB):</strong> Emirates, flydubai — most frequent connections globally</li>
        <li><strong>Doha (DOH):</strong> Qatar Airways — excellent Europe/USA network</li>
        <li><strong>Abu Dhabi (AUH):</strong> Etihad Airways — US pre-clearance for Americans</li>
        <li><strong>Istanbul (IST):</strong> Turkish Airlines — vast network, often cheaper</li>
        <li><strong>Riyadh/Jeddah (RUH/JED):</strong> Saudia — strong Africa/Americas</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Pakistani Airlines on International Routes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>PIA (Pakistan International Airlines):</strong> Gulf, UK (Manchester, Birmingham), Toronto, select other long-haul</li>
        <li><strong>Airblue:</strong> Gulf and Saudi Arabia</li>
        <li><strong>Serene Air / AirSial / Fly Jinnah:</strong> primarily domestic + Gulf</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Baggage Allowance Tips</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Gulf carriers to USA/Canada:</strong> typically 2 x 23kg checked bags (46kg total)</li>
        <li><strong>Gulf carriers to Europe/UK:</strong> often just 1 x 30kg or 2 x 23kg depending on class</li>
        <li><strong>Economy to Saudi/UAE from Pakistan:</strong> usually 30kg total</li>
        <li><strong>Low-cost (flydubai, Airblue):</strong> 20kg standard, extras cost extra</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Always check <em>your specific ticket</em> — allowances vary by fare class even within the same airline.
      </p>

      <h2>Booking Platforms Pakistani Travellers Use</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Google Flights:</strong> best for comparing airlines quickly</li>
        <li><strong>Skyscanner:</strong> flexible dates, nearby airports</li>
        <li><strong>Booking.com / Kayak:</strong> package deals with hotels</li>
        <li><strong>Direct airline website:</strong> often best for changes/refunds</li>
        <li><strong>Local travel agents:</strong> good for Hajj, Umrah, group bookings</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Related Tools</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="/tools/pkr-currency-converter/">Currency Converter</a> ·
        <a href="/tools/travel-insurance-calculator/">Insurance Calculator</a> ·
        <a href="/tools/passport-validity-checker/">Passport Validity Checker</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
